hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24297","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, al-Rabi' ibn Sabrah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah al-Juhani, who said: I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Whoever is here from Ma'add, let him stand. He said: So I took my garment to stand, and he said: Sit. Then he said: Whoever is here from Ma'add, let him stand. He said: So I took my garment to stand, and he said: Sit. So he said it a third time, and I said: From whom are we, O Messenger of Allah? He said: From Himyar."
"24298","Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from al-Rabi' ibn Sabrah, I heard Amr ibn Murrah al-Juhani say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever is here from Ma'add, let him stand. So I stood, and he said: Sit. So he did that three times; each time I would stand and he would say: Sit. When it was the third time I said: From whom are we, O Messenger of Allah? He said: You, O company of Quda'ah, are from Himyar. Amr said: So I concealed this hadith for twenty years."
"24299","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah informed us, from Ubaydullah Ibn Abi Ja'far, from Isa ibn Talhah, from Amr ibn Murrah al-Juhani, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have borne witness that there is no god but Allah and that you are the Messenger of Allah, and I have prayed the five, given the zakah of my wealth, and fasted the month of Ramadan. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever dies upon this will be with the prophets, the truthful, and the martyrs on the Day of Resurrection, like this, and he set up his two fingers, so long as he does not disobey his parents."
"24300","Yazid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Ali al-Bunani, from Abu al-Hasan, from Amr ibn Murrah, that he said to Mu'awiyah: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no ruler who closes his door against one with need, want, and poverty, except Allah closes the doors of heaven against his need, want, and poverty."
